Change and reason:
The SSE reader now opens at the first data line and serves data through the lib stream face. It keeps a reusable chunk intake and at most one line piece instead of retaining an event, so peer event size no longer controls reader allocation. End and final dispatch metadata share the blank-line entry point; cut events fail data and never dispatch. Read withdrawal scans and drops the remainder; body terminals validate already delivered line tails before selecting their outcome.
Whole-event unit observers and the temporary LLM gatherer consume that face. HTTP/protocol stacks feed the tokenizer directly and publish decoded documents only after dispatch; shutdown routes the tokenizer withdrawal even after its Closed event. Intake::clear preserves capacity and resets cached scan progress to support data withdrawal without reallocation.
